---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../../data/site";

const updated = "24 September 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Snapzy Google Drive integration: privacy policy"
  description="How my personal Google Drive setup for the Snapzy screenshot app handles your data."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-12">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-[clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)] leading-[1.1] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em]">
      Snapzy Google Drive integration
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose mt-10">
      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/duongductrong/Snapzy">Snapzy</a> is an open-source screenshot app for macOS. It can
        upload captures to Google Drive using an OAuth client that the user supplies. This page covers the OAuth client
        named "Snapzy" that I, {site.name}, registered on Google Cloud for my own use. It is not an official Snapzy
        service, and it is not offered to the public.
      </p>

      <h2>Data the app accesses</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Drive files created by the app</strong> (scope <code>drive.file</code>). The app can only see and
          manage the files it uploads itself. It cannot read anything else in your Drive.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your email address</strong> (scope <code>userinfo.email</code>), shown in Snapzy so you know which
          account is connected.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the data is used</h2>
      <p>
        When you choose to upload a capture, Snapzy sends the file straight from your Mac to your Google Drive, into a
        folder named "Snapzy", and sets it to "anyone with the link can view" so the link can be shared. Sign-in tokens
        stay on your Mac. No data passes through any server of mine, and I do not collect, store, sell or share any of
        it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Removing access and data</h2>
      <p>
        Uploaded files live in your own Drive and can be deleted there at any time. To revoke the app's access, remove
        "Snapzy" at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this page: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
